{"base_rate":0.2851511169513798,"brier":0.21532641261498026,"bss":-0.056350360870154326,"bss_hi":0.1459388777117422,"bss_lo":-0.2787423859177191,"chart":{"base":[308.5,262.5],"fp":[171.1,34.1],"lead":"62,257.7 272,222.1 482,189.2 692,127.9","note":{"base":"skill -0.06 — higher than 8% of cities","fp":"low end -3pp, high end +40pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 61% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 0%; promised 98% → rained 62%"},"rel":"62.1,466 140.4,457.6 426.1,401.5 676.9,197.2"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.2509592641261498,"ess":473.9284681384354,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Sendai</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Sendai rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>72%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.06, ranked 199 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(164&ndash;205) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>145</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>234</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Sendai</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;29% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 29% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.06</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>164&ndash;205\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Sendai &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Sendai\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.073241379310346,379.4896551724138 73.2456,348.02666666666664 129.10975000000002,272.8 218.58324999999996,177.25 310.15324324324325,86.86486486486484 378.2487671232876,32.95890410958907 411.41,18.0 411.41,21.111111111111086 378.2487671232876,77.83561643835617 310.15324324324325,160.64864864864865 218.58324999999996,254.60000000000002 129.10975000000002,341.05 73.2456,382.0 58.073241379310346,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"278.20499342969777\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"278.20499342969777\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.073241379310346,382.0 73.2456,382.0 129.10975000000002,368.35 218.58324999999996,318.3 310.15324324324325,337.72972972972974 378.2487671232876,267.3150684931507 411.41,120.66666666666669\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 145 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"58.073241379310346\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"73.2456\" cy=\"382.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"129.10975000000002\" cy=\"368.35\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"218.58324999999996\" cy=\"318.3\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"310.15324324324325\" cy=\"337.72972972972974\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"378.2487671232876\" cy=\"267.3150684931507\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 72% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 234 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.41\" cy=\"120.66666666666669\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(29%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Sendai the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.45) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-1.50).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>-1.496</td><td class='num'>40.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>-0.082</td><td class='num'>27.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.133</td><td class='num'>20.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.448</td><td class='num'>14.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":38.26667,"lon":140.86667,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Sendai","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00020689655172413793,"n":145,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.04306666666666667,"n":75,"obs":0.0,"sig":false},{"hi":0.31,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.200875,"n":80,"obs":0.0375,"sig":true},{"hi":0.61,"lo":0.31,"mean":0.4536249999999999,"n":80,"obs":0.175,"sig":true},{"hi":0.82,"lo":0.61,"mean":0.7122972972972973,"n":74,"obs":0.12162162162162163,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.82,"mean":0.9046575342465752,"n":73,"obs":0.3150684931506849,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9983333333333334,"n":234,"obs":0.717948717948718,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.7,"provisional":false,"rank":199,"rank_hi":205.0,"rank_lo":164.0,"reliability":0.10259573556920554,"resolution":0.09151282808672213,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"sendai","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo"}